From c0857963153dbcd293939c381a530dab7a66e953 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:49:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 190/214] fix: never wrap a top-level CryFX function in a
 file-scope %-flag #if

RT_IsTriPixel and RT_GetFadedNormal sat between a file-scope `#if %_RT_QUALITY` and
its `#endif`, and that made RenderLightingCommonVS and BuildRayTracingLightListCS
fail to compile with "undeclared identifier 'IsDiffuseMode'".

The rule, from the parser:

  - CryFX strips unused code per entry point by REACHABILITY, but only for NAMED code
    fragments: InitShaderDependenciesList (ShaderFXParseBin.cpp:2070-2094) walks the
    entry function's token range, pulls in every eFT_Function / eFT_StorageClass whose
    name token it finds, and recurses.
  - ParserBin.cpp:2157-2171 turns every file-scope preprocessor directive into its own
    SCodeFragment and NEVER assigns m_dwName.
  - ParseBinFX_Technique_Pass_GenerateShaderData (ShaderFXParseBin.cpp:2961-2969)
    emits a fragment unconditionally when m_dwName is 0 - the reachability list is
    consulted only for named ones.

So a %-flag conditional region at file scope reaches every stage's generated script,
while the named helpers the code inside it calls are still stripped from the stages
that do not reach them. Plain #define guards (ENABLE_TESSELLATION, FEATURE_SVO_GI,
SVO_LMAPS, NV_VR_*) are safe because the real preprocessor resolves them before CryFX
ever tokenizes the file - which is why every stock file-scope guard around a top-level
function in this tree is one of those, and why this had never bitten before.

Left unwrapped, both helpers are ordinary named fragments: the pixel entry points that
call them pull them in, every other stage strips them, and RT_GetFadedNormal's ddx/ddy
never reach a stage with no derivatives. Their bodies compile in every permutation
(VOX_MAX_RT_* and SVO_RTParams1 are declared unconditionally), so no guard is needed.
A #if INSIDE a struct body or a function body stays as it was - CE's own
pixoutMRTUpscale and the %_PS blocks in CommonSVO.cfi are the precedent.

Shader only, no C++ change. rtharness2 re-run: 16 ps_5_0 compiles across
(QUALITY, SAMPLE6), (QUALITY, SAMPLE6, PARTICLE_SHADOW), (QUALITY) and (SAMPLE4),
plus the cs_5_0 light grid. 0 errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 .../Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi  |  3 +++
 .../HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx    | 24 +++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
index ce8570fc..fdebb221 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CommonSVO_RT.cfi
@@ -113,6 +113,9 @@ struct SRTInfo
 	// rt stage 2C, debug only: the raw tangent-space _ddna sample of the hit, before the
 	// distance fade and before the tangent-to-world rotation. Debug view 10 renders it, so a
 	// "flat normals" finding can be pinned on the atlas layer instead of on the fade.
+	// A #if INSIDE a struct body is safe - CE's own pixoutMRTUpscale does it
+	// (Total_Illumination.cfx:194-197). A #if at FILE SCOPE around a top-level function is
+	// not; see the warning above RT_IsTriPixel in Total_Illumination.cfx.
 	float4   dbgAtlasNormal;
 #endif
 
diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
index 2063607a..6a6e7b35 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
@@ -1009,7 +1009,28 @@ float GetBlendMin(float2 tc0, float2 tc1, float fAverSmoothness, float fDepth0,
 	return saturate(fMinBlend);
 }
 
-#if %_RT_QUALITY
+///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+// !!! DO NOT WRAP THESE TWO IN A FILE-SCOPE #if. !!!
+//
+// CryFX's dead-code stripping only reaches NAMED code fragments. ParserBin.cpp:2157-2171
+// turns every file-scope preprocessor directive into a code fragment whose m_dwName is never
+// assigned, and ShaderFXParseBin.cpp:2961-2969 copies every unnamed fragment into EVERY
+// stage's generated script without consulting the reachability list that
+// InitShaderDependenciesList (ShaderFXParseBin.cpp:2070-2094) built. A top-level function
+// sitting between a file-scope #if and its #endif therefore reaches the VS and the CS as
+// well, while the helpers it calls - which ARE named fragments - are correctly stripped from
+// them, and the stage fails with "undeclared identifier". That is exactly what
+// #if %_RT_QUALITY around RT_IsTriPixel did to RenderLightingCommonVS and
+// BuildRayTracingLightListCS: they got the body and not IsDiffuseMode (CommonSVO.cfi:226).
+//
+// Left unwrapped, both are ordinary named fragments: the pixel entry points that call them
+// pull them in, every other stage strips them, and RT_GetFadedNormal's ddx/ddy never reach a
+// stage that has no derivatives. This is how every function in CommonSVO_RT.cfi is written.
+// The only stock file-scope #if blocks around a top-level function in this tree are
+// `#ifdef SVO_LMAPS` (a plain define, never set) and Illum.cfx's `%SILHOUETTE_*` material
+// flag - no %_RT_ one, which is why nobody hit this before.
+///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
+
 ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 // rt stage 2C: the ONE predicate that decides "this pixel is traced with triangles".
 //
@@ -1053,7 +1074,6 @@ float3 RT_GetFadedNormal(const float3 vPos0, const float3 vNor0, const float fDi
 
 	return normalize(lerp(vFlat, vNor0, RT_GetNormalsFade(fDistM)));
 }
-#endif
 
 #define SVO_MAX_PORTALS 8
 
